From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: cancel scan timeout when dropping a scan vdev

[ SBE1V1K: our addition on top of "wifi: ath12k: convert scan timeout to
  wiphy delayed work" (943, the posted v4). Kept as a separate patch at
  the end of the series because folding it into 943 would change the
  context of 945, which then no longer applies without fuzz. Requires
  943. ]

The hw_scan abort path in ath12k_mac_op_hw_scan() and
ath12k_mac_op_remove_interface() reset a radio's scan state to IDLE and
drop ar->scan.arvif, but only cancel ar->scan.vdev_clean_wk. A scan
timeout that was queued for a scan that has already started stays
pending and fires later, possibly after a new scan has been started on
the same radio, which it would then abort.

Cancel ar->scan.timeout next to vdev_clean_wk in both places. Both run
with the wiphy mutex held, as wiphy_delayed_work_cancel() requires.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -5954,6 +5954,7 @@ abort:
 
 			if (ar->scan.arvif == arvif) {
 				wiphy_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.vdev_clean_wk);
+				wiphy_delayed_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.timeout);
 				spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 				ar->scan.arvif = NULL;
 				ar->scan.state = ATH12K_SCAN_IDLE;
@@ -11185,6 +11186,7 @@ void ath12k_mac_op_remove_interface(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		 */
 		if (ar->scan.arvif == arvif) {
 			wiphy_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.vdev_clean_wk);
+			wiphy_delayed_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.timeout);
 
 			spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 			ar->scan.arvif = NULL;
